index c467113..c7921ac 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/gateway-middleware.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/gateway-middleware.md
@@ -28,6 +28,31 @@ plugins.json is the source of truth for which middleware is installed and on, in
 5. `Run.Wrap` wraps the response writer when some middleware has `onEvent` or `onResponse`. An SSE reply is split into events. Each event whose data is a JSON object goes to every `onEvent` that wants its name (`export const events`): an object replaces it, `null` drops it, and `undefined` writes the original bytes. `data: [DONE]` and other non-object data pass by. A whole JSON reply is buffered for `onResponse`, with `ctx.status` set. A reply with a `Content-Encoding` passes as-is.
 6. `Run.End` returns the runtimes to their pools.
 
+### Provider-error recovery
+
+`Run.ProviderError` invokes `onProviderError(body, ctx)` after an explicit
+Azure resource or encrypted-content validation failure, before normal
+fallback. `ctx.provider.recoverySupported` advertises support. The host sets
+`ctx.failure` with `kind`, `status`, `attempt:1`, `outputStarted:false` and an
+optional rejected `itemID`; raw errors, headers and credentials are omitted.
+
+Return `undefined` for existing host handling, `{action:"stop"}` to return
+the failed response, or `{action:"retry",body}` to retry once. Only `input`,
+`store` and `previous_response_id` may change. The retry uses the same
+provider/account/model through the normal lane and budget checks; it does
+not replace shared history or establish a persistent cleanup flag. A failed
+repair returns an error rather than running another recovery or fallback.
+
+The gateway requires no output, reasoning or tool activity, an active client,
+and `errors` other than `pass`. Held SSE failures and HTTP validation errors
+use the same path. Generic server/auth/quota/timeout/safety errors do not
+trigger this interface. `ctx.failure` is cleared after the callback.
+
+`serveAgentMiddleware` is the shared JS chain for ordinary agent requests
+and `codexCompact` text-summary attempts. Summary attempts do not reenter
+conversation recording or asynchronous gateway hooks. Native checkpoint
+decryption and the standalone compact endpoint keep their original paths.
+
 Each middleware gets one runtime for the whole request, so its hooks share `ctx.state`. Runtimes come from a per-middleware `sync.Pool` and modules are compiled once per load. Compiling a plugin's module (imports kept inside the plugin) is [`internal/jsmod`](../../internal/jsmod/jsmod.go), which agent plugins ([Agent wiring](agent-wiring.md)) share.
 
 Only requests agents send go through `serveAgent`. magpie's own requests (thread titles, the router's classifier, the search and vision stand-ins) call `serve` directly. A search or an image's description asked while an agent's request is served is made on that request's context, and takes the request's middleware off it (`ownAsk`): the runtimes are the request's, which one goroutine may use at a time (moejs), and `Run` has no lock to hold callers to it, and these asks go beside it and each other, so images described at once ran `onProvider` on one runtime and the gateway died of `concurrent map read and map write`. Nor does the hooks' `ctx` describe them: a description's body is Chat and a search's Anthropic, whatever `ctx.protocol` names, and `ctx.model` and `ctx.stream` are the agent's (#3695, `TestImagesDescribedWithoutTheAgentsMiddleware`, `TestSearchesWithoutTheAgentsMiddleware`). Middleware sees bodies before redaction, which still applies upstream, through the `redact` plugin's masker; masking asked for with no masker serving sends nothing ([Plugin runtime](plugin-runtime.md)).
